---

<section id="story" class="scroll-mt-24 bg-paper py-20 sm:py-24">
  <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl items-center gap-12 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:grid-cols-2">
    <div class="relative pb-8">
      <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-3xl shadow-(--shadow-lift)">
        <img
          src="/images/van-camp.jpg"
          alt="A camper van parked in nature"
          class="aspect-[4/3] w-full object-cover"
        />
      </div>
      <div
        class="absolute -bottom-6 -right-2 hidden w-48 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border-4 border-paper shadow-(--shadow-card) sm:block lg:-right-8"
      >
        <img src="/images/nature-camp.jpg" alt="A quiet campsite among trees" class="aspect-square w-full object-cover" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <div>
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-blue">Our story</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-navy sm:text-4xl">
        We are Beatriz and Eelco. Vanlife is how we live.
      </h2>
      <div class="mt-6 space-y-4 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-navy/75">
        <p>
          For more than eight years we have been travelling in a van. park4night has been our
          compass: a farm in Portugal, a quiet forest track in Sweden, a night by the sea that we
          still talk about.
        </p>
        <p>
          Lately, more and more of those parking places look different. Plastic in the hedges.
          Human waste a few metres from the pitch. Fire rings full of cans. Beautiful spots that
          get closed because a few people could not take their rubbish with them.
        </p>
        <p>
          We started <strong class="font-semibold text-navy">clean4park</strong> to create more
          awareness. Clean up after yourself. Leave places cleaner than you found them. That is how
          we — and everyone who loves this community — can keep enjoying park4night for many more
          years.
        </p>
      </div>
      <blockquote
        class="mt-8 border-l-4 border-mint pl-5 text-lg font-medium leading-snug text-navy"
      >
        “The next van should find it better than we did.”
      </blockquote>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
